# Citation metadata for the arena as software and protocol. GitHub reads this
# file and offers "Cite this repository". The authors here are the people who
# built and run the arena; the papers that come out of it carry their own
# bylines and will be added under preferred-citation when they are public.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Social Simulation Arena, its protocol, or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Social Simulation Arena"
abstract: "A live benchmark for social simulation. Entrants forecast published population statistics before release; forecasts lock and are timestamped before the answer exists, and the released number scores them in public against a persistence baseline."
authors:
